{
  "$comment": [
    "Policy for the fully unattended issue-to-merge loop. See",
    "docs/loop-engineering.md#fully-unattended-mode.",
    "",
    "The governing idea: risk decides HOW MUCH VERIFICATION a change must pass,",
    "not WHETHER A HUMAN IS SUMMONED. All three tiers can merge automatically.",
    "They differ only in what has to be true first.",
    "",
    "This file is data, not code, so a reviewer can audit the whole merge policy",
    "by reading it. It is part of the control plane, so changing it is always",
    "high risk, always dual-reviewed, and additionally checked for whether the",
    "change WEAKENS a protection rather than merely altering one."
  ],
  "retry": {
    "$comment": [
      "Bounded per category. Exhausting one blocks that issue and the loop moves",
      "to independent work \u2014 a single stuck issue is never a global stop."
    ],
    "maxReviewAttempts": 3,
    "codingFixRounds": 3,
    "reviewFixRounds": 3,
    "ciFixRounds": 3,
    "reviewerRetryRounds": 2,
    "conflictRounds": 2
  },
  "risk": {
    "default": "low",
    "$comment": [
      "Every changed path is matched against every rule; the HIGHEST matching",
      "risk wins. Matching upward rather than by specificity means a new file",
      "under a sensitive directory is protected by default, and a mistake in a",
      "pattern fails safe.",
      "",
      "AGENTS.md and docs/loop-engineering.md are deliberately NOT listed here.",
      "They are handled by controlPlane.policySignals: a diff that changes what",
      "the rules SAY is policy and goes high; a diff that corrects a command or",
      "a path is documentation and goes medium."
    ],
    "paths": [
      {
        "risk": "high",
        "reason": "repository automation, CI, and merge policy",
        "patterns": [".github/**", "tooling/loop/**", "tooling/local-runner/**"]
      },
      {
        "risk": "high",
        "reason": "infrastructure with cross-service blast radius",
        "patterns": ["infra/**", "docker-compose*.yml", ".dockerignore"]
      },
      {
        "risk": "high",
        "reason": "authentication and authorization architecture",
        "patterns": ["packages/auth/**", "apps/api/src/rpc/identity.ts"]
      },
      {
        "risk": "high",
        "reason": "architecture invariants",
        "patterns": ["docs/architecture.md", "docs/adr/**"]
      },
      {
        "risk": "high",
        "reason": "environment and secret handling",
        "patterns": [".env.example", "**/.env*"]
      },
      {
        "risk": "medium",
        "reason": "application and shared library code",
        "patterns": ["apps/**", "packages/**", "e2e/**", "scripts/**", "tooling/**"]
      },
      {
        "risk": "medium",
        "reason": "workspace and toolchain configuration",
        "patterns": [
          "package.json",
          "*/package.json",
          "*/*/package.json",
          "bun.lock",
          "turbo.json",
          "biome.json",
          "tsconfig.base.json"
        ]
      },
      {
        "risk": "medium",
        "reason": "documentation that can carry policy (see controlPlane.policySignals)",
        "patterns": ["AGENTS.md", "docs/loop-engineering.md", "docs/local-agent-runner.md"]
      },
      {
        "risk": "low",
        "reason": "documentation",
        "patterns": ["docs/**", "README.md", "*.md"]
      }
    ],
    "escalations": {
      "$comment": [
        "Deterministic conditions that raise risk regardless of path. Each is",
        "computed from the diff, never from model judgement."
      ],
      "maxChangedFiles": 40,
      "maxDeletedLines": 600,
      "destructiveMigrationGlobs": ["packages/db/drizzle/**/*.sql"],
      "publicContractGlobs": ["packages/api-contract/src/**"]
    }
  },
  "tiers": {
    "$comment": [
      "Cumulative: medium inherits low, high inherits medium. A step with",
      "`whenChanged` runs only when the diff touches something it could break.",
      "A step with `requires` needs that tool on PATH \u2014 and if it is missing the",
      "step is UNAVAILABLE, which blocks the issue. It is never counted as",
      "passed, because 'could not check' and 'checked, fine' are different",
      "answers and only one of them justifies a merge."
    ],
    "low": {
      "reviewers": 1,
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "format",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "format"],
          "timeoutMinutes": 5
        },
        {
          "name": "lint",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "lint"],
          "timeoutMinutes": 5
        },
        {
          "name": "typecheck",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "typecheck"],
          "timeoutMinutes": 10
        },
        {
          "name": "test",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "test"],
          "timeoutMinutes": 20
        },
        {
          "name": "build",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "build"],
          "timeoutMinutes": 20
        }
      ]
    },
    "medium": {
      "inherits": "low",
      "reviewers": 1,
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "dependency-audit",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["install", "--frozen-lockfile", "--dry-run"],
          "whenChanged": ["**/package.json", "bun.lock"],
          "timeoutMinutes": 5
        },
        {
          "name": "e2e",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "test:e2e"],
          "whenChanged": [
            "apps/**",
            "e2e/**",
            "packages/api-contract/**",
            "packages/api-client/**"
          ],
          "requires": "docker",
          "timeoutMinutes": 30,
          "requiresProbe": ["docker", "info"]
        }
      ]
    },
    "high": {
      "inherits": "medium",
      "reviewers": 2,
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "docker-smoke",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "docker:smoke"],
          "whenChanged": ["infra/**", "docker-compose*.yml", "apps/**", "packages/db/**"],
          "requires": "docker",
          "timeoutMinutes": 30,
          "requiresProbe": ["docker", "info"]
        },
        {
          "name": "load-balancing",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "verify:lb"],
          "whenChanged": ["infra/**", "docker-compose*.yml", "apps/api/**"],
          "requires": "docker",
          "timeoutMinutes": 10,
          "requiresProbe": ["docker", "info"]
        },
        {
          "name": "migration",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "db:migrate"],
          "whenChanged": ["packages/db/**"],
          "requires": "docker",
          "timeoutMinutes": 15,
          "requiresProbe": ["docker", "info"]
        },
        {
          "name": "loop-self-test",
          "command": "bun",
          "args": ["run", "--filter", "@newsdeck/loop", "test"],
          "whenChanged": [".github/**", "tooling/loop/**", "tooling/local-runner/**"],
          "timeoutMinutes": 10
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "controlPlane": {
    "$comment": [
      "The rules the loop uses to govern itself. A change here gets the full",
      "treatment regardless of how small it looks, and is additionally checked",
      "for whether it WEAKENS a protection.",
      "",
      "policySignals are matched against the ADDED AND REMOVED LINES of a diff,",
      "not the file. That is what separates 'fix a stale command in AGENTS.md'",
      "(medium, ordinary) from 'change what AGENTS.md says agents may merge'",
      "(high, control plane). Case-insensitive."
    ],
    "patterns": [
      ".github/workflows/**",
      ".github/loop-policy.json",
      ".github/loop-dependencies.json",
      "tooling/loop/**",
      "tooling/local-runner/src/orchestrator.ts",
      "tooling/local-runner/src/github.ts",
      "tooling/local-runner/prompts/**"
    ],
    "alwaysPolicy": [".github/loop-policy.json", ".github/workflows/loop-*.yml"],
    "policySignals": [
      "auto[- ]?merge",
      "merge gate",
      "required check",
      "branch protection",
      "ruleset",
      "human approval",
      "risk:(low|medium|high)",
      "risk classification",
      "blocking severity",
      "permission[- ]?mode",
      "allowedTools",
      "bypassPermissions",
      "force[- ]?push",
      "must never",
      "safety invariant",
      "control plane",
      "agent:(ready|blocked|in-progress|review)",
      "reviewers"
    ]
  },
  "review": {
    "$comment": [
      "Findings at or above this severity block an automatic merge. Lower",
      "severities are reported but do not hold the pull request.",
      "",
      "Reviewer count is per tier, under `tiers`. High risk takes two",
      "independent passes with no shared session."
    ],
    "blockingSeverity": "high"
  },
  "requiredChecks": ["Lint and types", "Tests", "Build", "loop/risk-gate", "loop/review-gate"]
}
